      "bank_transfers": "Settlement operates on batch cycles or messaging networks (ACH takes 1-3 business days; SEPA takes 1 business day; SEPA Instant and FedNow offer near-instant settlement). Settlement is legally final after clearing window closure, but remains subject to chargebacks or reversals (e.g., 60-day window for ACH fraud disputes).",
      "wallet_transfers": "Settlement occurs on-chain with deterministic finality within seconds or minutes depending on the network. For example, Layer 2 networks like Lisk (built on the OP Stack), Base, and Arbitrum provide soft finality in milliseconds via sequencers and hard settlement finality once batches post to Ethereum Layer 1. Transactions are irreversible once confirmed."
    },
    {
      "metric": "Transaction Fees & Cost Structure",
      "bank_transfers": "Fixed or percentage-based gateway and intermediary fees (typically 0.5% to 3% for credit/debit, $0.20 to $1.50 for ACH, $15 to $40 for wire/SWIFT). Interchange and banking platform overhead dominate the cost model.",
      "wallet_transfers": "Network execution (gas) fees paid to validators/sequencers. On high-throughput networks and EVM Layer 2s such as Lisk, Polygon PoS, or Optimism, network fees are fractions of a cent ($0.001 - $0.05), independent of transaction size, though fiat on/off-ramp aggregators introduce a 0.5% - 2.5% fee spread."
